Package: bifrost-emu
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ca-certificates, curl, python3, xz-utils
Recommends: libsdl3-0 (>= 3.2.0), libgl1, libwayland-client0, libx11-6
Description: run AArch64 Linux programs and Android apps on x86-64
 bifrost-emu is a user-mode AArch64 emulator with a JIT compiler. It runs
 ARM64 Linux programs and games (graphics, audio and input go to the host's
 libraries) and, with the separate Asgard layer, Android apps.
 .
 Dynamically linked programs need a guest root filesystem: run
 "bifrost-emu --setup-rootfs" once. It downloads the glibc and musl toolchains
 (about 235 MB) and builds a rootfs under ~/.local/share/bifrost.
 "bifrost-emu --setup-rootfs --games" adds a profile with the libraries Linux games
 need. Android windows need libsdl3-0 3.2 or newer.

Package: bifrost-emu-asgard
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         bifrost-emu (= ${binary:Version}),
         binutils,
         ca-certificates,
         clang,
         curl,
         default-jdk-headless,
         e2fsprogs,
         lld,
         python3,
         xz-utils
Recommends: libsdl3-0 (>= 3.2.0)
Description: Asgard, the Android layer of bifrost-emu: setup tooling
 Asgard runs Android apps (.apk, .apkm, .apks, .xapk) on bifrost-emu with a real
 Bionic, ART and the Android 15 framework. This package holds the tooling and
 the one command that sets it up: "asgard-setup" downloads the pinned Android
 pieces (about 1.5 GB, checked by hash), builds the adapters and launcher and
 installs Asgard under ~/.local (about 1.1 GB). Nothing from Google or the
 Android Open Source Project is shipped in the package itself.
 .
 Afterwards "bifrost-emu app.apk" installs and runs an app from any directory.
 Android windows need libsdl3-0 3.2 or newer.
